# Prebuilt libmetal / open-amp archives (SoC repo)

The third-party archives + the upstream header trees (../include) + the
license texts live in this repo (device_soc_rockchip); the kernel repo
(kernel/liteos_m/components/openamp) only references them from its build
files - no third-party text or binaries are stored there. The
self-developed libmica tree (kernel/liteos_m/compat/mcs/mica) and the
libmetal "liteos" system backend source (../include/libmetal/system/liteos/
metal_sys.c, part of this repo's header tree) are compiled from source by
the kernel repo's openamp component - no archive is shipped for them.

Upstream provenance (vanilla snapshots, unmodified upstream sources):

| archive        | upstream   | objects (link order)                                            |
|----------------|------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------|
| `libmetal.a`   | v1.3.0     | init, device, io, log                                           |
| `openamp.a`    | v1.3.1     | virtio, virtqueue, remoteproc_virtio, rpmsg, rpmsg_virtio      |

Toolchain/flags used to build them (must match to regenerate bit-identical
objects):

    aarch64-liteos-clang (OHOS clang 15.0.4, prebuilts/clang/ohos/linux-x86_64/llvm)
    --target=aarch64-linux-ohos -mcpu=cortex-a55 -mgeneral-regs-only
    -ffreestanding -nostdlib -O2 -fdata-sections -ffunction-sections
    -fno-builtin -fsigned-char -std=c99
    include: ../include/libmetal  + generated metal/system/liteos backend

## Why prebuilt

The third_party source snapshots (third_party/libmetal, third_party/open-amp)
are not shipped: introducing third-party source requires a separate
review/approval. The compiled objects plus the public headers are sufficient
for the rk3568_m AMP build; everything else (the libmetal liteos system
backend, the self-developed libmica) is compiled from source by
kernel/liteos_m/components/openamp.

## Regeneration recipe

- libmetal v1.3.0 core headers : ../include/libmetal/ (top-level + compiler/gcc
  + processor/aarch64 + system/liteos backend incl. metal_sys.c)
- open-amp v1.3.1 headers      : ../include/open-amp/
- libmica (self-developed)     : kernel/liteos_m/compat/mcs/mica/
  (sources + platform headers, compiled from source - no archive)

To regenerate the archives: build rk3568_m with a kernel_liteos_m
components/openamp/BUILD.gn that compiles libmetal/open-amp from source
(e.g. the revision before the prebuilt switch), and re-archive from out/
keeping the exact member order recorded at the top of this file.

## Header trees

- The public header trees live in this repo at
  //device/soc/rockchip/rk3568_m/include/{libmetal,open-amp} (same upstream
  provenance: libmetal v1.3.0 lib/ .h subset, open-amp v1.3.1 lib/include).
  The kernel repo's build references them there (see
  kernel/liteos_m/components/openamp/{BUILD.gn,mcs_includes.gni}).

Licenses: BSD-3-Clause (libmetal) / BSD-2-Clause with parts BSD-3-Clause
(open-amp) - the license texts live next to the headers:
//device/soc/rockchip/rk3568_m/include/LICENSE.{libmetal,open-amp}.
